{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.721163f423","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data3-128","passage":"<p>The discovery of the letter proved ______, changing how historians understood the entire war.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["routine","trivial","hypothetical","pivotal"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “pivotal,” meaning extremely important. “Routine” (ordinary) doesn't fit. “Hypothetical” (imagined) doesn't fit. “Trivial” (of little importance) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.420bdbb2df","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data3-131","passage":"<p>Critics met the artist's first exhibit with ______, calling it childish and pointless.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["acclaim","controversy","indifference","scorn"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “scorn,” meaning open contempt. “Indifference” (lack of interest) doesn't fit. “Acclaim” (enthusiastic praise) doesn't fit. “Controversy” (public disagreement) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.fec45dab68","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data3-138","passage":"<p>The encyclopedia's ______ entry covered every known species in the family.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["biased","nuanced","simplistic","exhaustive"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “exhaustive,” meaning comprehensive. “Biased” (one-sided) doesn't fit. “Nuanced” (showing subtle differences) doesn't fit. “Simplistic” (oversimplified) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7c329a747e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data3-143","passage":"<p>As a ______ at chess, Leo still confused the moves of the bishop and the knight.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["rival","novice","veteran","mentor"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “novice,” meaning beginner. “Rival” (competitor) doesn't fit. “Mentor” (experienced adviser) doesn't fit. “Veteran” (person with long experience) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a2d1eb120c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-147","passage":"<p>The coral reef proved surprisingly ______, regrowing within a decade after a severe storm.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["pliable","brittle","resilient","porous"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “resilient,” meaning able to recover quickly. “Porous” (full of tiny holes) doesn't fit. “Brittle” (hard but easily broken) doesn't fit. “Pliable” (easily bent) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.1633f83c71","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-149","passage":"<p>The new ramp will ______ access for visitors who use wheelchairs.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["facilitate","hinder","prohibit","mandate"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “facilitate,” meaning make easier. “Hinder” (get in the way of) doesn't fit. “Prohibit” (forbid) doesn't fit. “Mandate” (officially require) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b47534aa2f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-156","passage":"<p>A ______ scent of smoke lingered in the room long after the fire was out.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["faint","vivid","blurred","stark"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “faint,” meaning barely perceptible. “Blurred” (unclear in outline) doesn't fit. “Stark” (sharply clear and harsh) doesn't fit. “Vivid” (strikingly bright or detailed) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.6b4eacd89a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-162","passage":"<p>Diplomats must be ______ in their public statements, choosing every word carefully.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["circumspect","audacious","resolute","ambivalent"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “circumspect,” meaning cautious and careful. “Resolute” (firmly determined) doesn't fit. “Ambivalent” (having mixed feelings) doesn't fit. “Audacious” (boldly daring) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.548e93bc7e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-163","passage":"<p>Over many years, layers of sediment ______ at the bottom of the lake.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["assemble","attribute","allocate","accumulate"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “accumulate,” meaning gather over time. “Allocate” (distribute for a purpose) doesn't fit. “Assemble” (put together) doesn't fit. “Attribute” (regard as caused by) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.880e517ec8","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-170","passage":"<p>The city will ______ a new recycling program next month.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["sustain","suspend","initiate","conclude"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “initiate,” meaning begin. “Sustain” (keep going) doesn't fit. “Suspend” (temporarily stop) doesn't fit. “Conclude” (bring to an end) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a95144cf19","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-171","passage":"<p>The ______ passenger talked nonstop for the entire six-hour flight.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["garrulous","aloof","taciturn","affable"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “garrulous,” meaning excessively talkative. “Taciturn” (saying little) doesn't fit. “Affable” (friendly and easy to talk to) doesn't fit. “Aloof” (distant and reserved) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.0cd08df5cc","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-172","passage":"<p>Event organizers ______ that more than ten thousand people will attend the festival.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["overlook","anticipate","recall","postpone"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “anticipate,” meaning expect or predict. “Postpone” (delay) doesn't fit. “Overlook” (fail to notice) doesn't fit. “Recall” (remember) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.2089ac705f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-177","passage":"<p>The court can ______ a witness to testify, even if the witness would rather stay silent.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["deter","entice","compel","persuade"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “compel,” meaning force. “Persuade” (convince) doesn't fit. “Deter” (discourage) doesn't fit. “Entice” (attract by offering something) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.86945898a6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-178","passage":"<p>New data may ______ the scientist, whose theory was dismissed for decades.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["incriminate","implicate","exonerate","vindicate"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “vindicate,” meaning show to be right. “Implicate” (show to be involved) doesn't fit. “Incriminate” (make appear guilty) doesn't fit. “Exonerate” (clear of blame) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.1078368fbb","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-179","passage":"<p>The city's ______ population speaks more than eighty languages.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["diverse","scarce","homogeneous","prevalent"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “diverse,” meaning varied. “Prevalent” (widespread) doesn't fit. “Scarce” (in short supply) doesn't fit. “Homogeneous” (all of the same kind) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ff3dc14c24","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-181","passage":"<p>Without water, the seedlings began to ______ within a few days.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["thrive","wither","migrate","adapt"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “wither,” meaning shrivel and decline. “Adapt” (adjust to new conditions) doesn't fit. “Thrive” (grow vigorously) doesn't fit. “Migrate” (move from one region to another) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a4ad598dc9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-183","passage":"<p>Despite her fame, the author lives in ______ apartment with simple furniture.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a lavish","a sparse","an ornate","a modest"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “modest,” meaning not excessive. “Ornate” (elaborately decorated) doesn't fit. “Lavish” (extravagantly rich) doesn't fit. “Sparse” (thinly scattered) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.d0882dbefa","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-185","passage":"<p>The essay presented a ______ argument, with each point building logically on the last.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["verbose","fragmented","coherent","concise"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “coherent,” meaning logically connected. “Verbose” (using too many words) doesn't fit. “Fragmented” (broken into pieces) doesn't fit. “Concise” (brief but complete) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ba2d53437c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data4-188","passage":"<p>The city repaired the levee early to ______ flooding during the rainy season.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["preclude","forestall","entail","necessitate"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “forestall,” meaning prevent by acting first. “Necessitate” (make necessary) doesn't fit. “Entail” (involve as a necessary part) doesn't fit. “Preclude” (prevent from happening) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.de0a9aeb5d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-190","passage":"<p>The museum displays ______ of the ancient crown, since the original is too fragile to exhibit.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a prototype","a replica","an authentic","a counterfeit"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “replica,” meaning a copy made openly. “Authentic” (genuine) doesn't fit. “Counterfeit” (fake and meant to deceive) doesn't fit. “Prototype” (an early model) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9ad287e687","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-195","passage":"<p>Words like \"thou\" and \"thee\" sound ______ to modern readers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["colloquial","esoteric","ubiquitous","archaic"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “archaic,” meaning no longer in common use. “Colloquial” (informal and conversational) doesn't fit. “Esoteric” (understood by only a few) doesn't fit. “Ubiquitous” (found everywhere) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.6dffaae101","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-198","passage":"<p>After years without a fire, the town grew ______ and stopped maintaining its fire trucks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["indolent","zealous","industrious","complacent"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “complacent,” meaning self-satisfied and unaware of danger. “Industrious” (hardworking) doesn't fit. “Indolent” (lazy) doesn't fit. “Zealous” (passionately devoted) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9526c34a1b","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-204","passage":"<p>In the 1990s, online shopping was a ______ industry that few retailers took seriously.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["burgeoning","defunct","moribund","nascent"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “nascent,” meaning just beginning to develop. “Moribund” (near the end of existence) doesn't fit. “Defunct” (no longer existing) doesn't fit. “Burgeoning” (growing rapidly) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.8e14cafb89","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-205","passage":"<p>The negotiations turned ______ when both sides began shouting accusations.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["hostile","bold","timid","courteous"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “hostile,” meaning unfriendly and aggressive. “Courteous” (polite) doesn't fit. “Bold” (confident and daring) doesn't fit. “Timid” (shy and lacking courage) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9c230a6c1f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-207","passage":"<p>The calm lake seemed to ______ every tree on the shore.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["distort","illuminate","reflect","obscure"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “reflect,” meaning show an image of. “Distort” (twist out of shape) doesn't fit. “Obscure” (hide or make unclear) doesn't fit. “Illuminate” (light up or clarify) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.5dd27f355f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-209","passage":"<p>She caught only ______ glimpse of the deer before it vanished into the woods.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a latent","an evident","a hidden","a fleeting"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “fleeting,” meaning lasting a very short time. “Hidden” (kept out of sight) doesn't fit. “Evident” (clearly seen) doesn't fit. “Latent” (present but not yet developed) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.74965866eb","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-212","passage":"<p>The ______ rabbit froze at the edge of the field, too frightened to move.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["timorous","prudent","reckless","intrepid"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “timorous,” meaning fearful. “Intrepid” (fearless) doesn't fit. “Reckless” (careless of danger) doesn't fit. “Prudent” (wise and cautious) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.bcb20d35c6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-215","passage":"<p>A ______ researcher, she double-checked every source before publishing her article.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["punctual","tardy","diligent","careless"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “diligent,” meaning hardworking and careful. “Tardy” (late) doesn't fit. “Careless” (not paying attention) doesn't fit. “Punctual” (on time) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.3191d741bc","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-215","passage":"<p>A ______ mistake in the calculation caused the bridge's design to be rejected.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["punctual","diligent","tardy","careless"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “careless,” meaning not paying attention. “Diligent” (hardworking and careful) doesn't fit. “Tardy” (late) doesn't fit. “Punctual” (on time) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.2f3735b89b","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-217","passage":"<p>The storm caused a ______ power outage, leaving half the town without electricity.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["comprehensive","partial","brief","vague"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “partial,” meaning incomplete. “Vague” (unclear) doesn't fit. “Brief” (short) doesn't fit. “Comprehensive” (including everything) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b72a1e849c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-219","passage":"<p>The ______ rain stopped and started all afternoon, never lasting more than ten minutes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["temporary","constant","intermittent","persistent"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “intermittent,” meaning stopping and starting. “Persistent” (continuing firmly) doesn't fit. “Constant” (continuous) doesn't fit. “Temporary” (lasting a short time) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.90ceaaf5e1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-221","passage":"<p>The town was ______ to the volunteers who helped clean up after the flood.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["grateful","stingy","resentful","generous"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “grateful,” meaning thankful. “Generous” (giving freely) doesn't fit. “Stingy” (unwilling to share) doesn't fit. “Resentful” (feeling bitterness) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.8a198f723a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-222","passage":"<p>It seems ______ that adding a new road can sometimes make traffic worse, but studies show it happens.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["paradoxical","redundant","inevitable","plausible"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “paradoxical,” meaning seemingly contradictory but possibly true. “Inevitable” (certain to happen) doesn't fit. “Redundant” (unnecessarily repeated) doesn't fit. “Plausible” (seeming reasonable) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7be3d702a4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-225","passage":"<p>Tenants must ______ the building by Friday so repairs can begin.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["inhabit","commute","relocate","vacate"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “vacate,” meaning leave empty. “Inhabit” (live in) doesn't fit. “Relocate” (move to a new place) doesn't fit. “Commute” (travel regularly to work) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.2d829a3100","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-230","passage":"<p>That the shortest distance between two points is a straight line is treated as ______ in basic geometry.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a fallacy","a veracity","a conjecture","an axiom"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “axiom,” meaning self-evident truth. “Veracity” (truthfulness) doesn't fit. “Fallacy” (mistaken belief) doesn't fit. “Conjecture” (conclusion formed without proof) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.64f2dca171","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data5-231","passage":"<p>Without shelter, many animals ______ during the harsh winter.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["decline","perish","revive","flourish"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “perish,” meaning die. “Revive” (bring back to life or use) doesn't fit. “Flourish” (grow successfully) doesn't fit. “Decline” (decrease gradually) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.5ebf6738b1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-233","passage":"<p>Over many years, the diplomat worked to ______ friendships with leaders across the region.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["arrest","entertain","cultivate","appreciate"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “cultivate,” meaning develop over time. “Appreciate” (increase in value) doesn't fit. “Entertain” (consider) doesn't fit. “Arrest” (stop the progress of) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.11b9ccd4c2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-234","passage":"<p>The poet's ______ style uses few adjectives and no unnecessary words.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["grave","fair","spare","novel"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “spare,” meaning plain and without excess. “Novel” (new and original) doesn't fit. “Fair” (pale in color) doesn't fit. “Grave” (serious) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.36e99cdc7f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-235","passage":"<p>She spoke with such ______ that even her critics believed she meant every word.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["tender","reservation","conviction","charge"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “conviction,” meaning firm belief. “Reservation” (doubt) doesn't fit. “Charge” (responsibility or duty) doesn't fit. “Tender” (offer formally) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a42e9f781e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-240","passage":"<p>Many internet trends are ______, popular for a week and then forgotten.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["enduring","sporadic","cyclical","ephemeral"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “ephemeral,” meaning lasting a very short time. “Sporadic” (occurring at irregular intervals) doesn't fit. “Cyclical” (recurring in a regular pattern) doesn't fit. “Enduring” (long-lasting) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.0178c37db2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-241","passage":"<p>The company tried to ______ the product recall, calling it a minor precaution.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["downplay","highlight","disguise","expose"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “downplay,” meaning make seem less important. “Highlight” (draw attention to) doesn't fit. “Disguise” (hide the identity of) doesn't fit. “Expose” (reveal) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.520c9755ee","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-244","passage":"<p>The senate voted to ______ the member for misusing public funds, though he kept his seat.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["rescind","sanction","ratify","censure"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “censure,” meaning formally criticize. “Sanction” (officially approve) doesn't fit. “Rescind” (cancel officially) doesn't fit. “Ratify” (formally approve a treaty or agreement) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a5af1d57a0","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-245","passage":"<p>Old paper becomes ______ and can crumble at the slightest touch.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["elastic","flexible","rigid","brittle"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “brittle,” meaning hard but easily broken. “Elastic” (able to stretch and return to shape) doesn't fit. “Flexible” (able to change or adapt easily) doesn't fit. “Rigid” (unable to bend) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9c5483528a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-245","passage":"<p>The ______ waistband stretches to fit and then snaps back into place.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["flexible","elastic","rigid","brittle"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “elastic,” meaning able to stretch and return to shape. “Flexible” (able to change or adapt easily) doesn't fit. “Rigid” (unable to bend) doesn't fit. “Brittle” (hard but easily broken) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.e8fb4cbf53","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-246","passage":"<p>Oil prices have been ______ this year, jumping and falling sharply from week to week.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["capricious","volatile","tenacious","phlegmatic"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “volatile,” meaning liable to change rapidly. “Capricious” (unpredictable) doesn't fit. “Tenacious” (persistent and determined) doesn't fit. “Phlegmatic” (calm and unemotional) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.04a4a92cbd","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-248","passage":"<p>The heavy backpack was more of ______ than a help on the steep climb.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a catalyst","a hindrance","an impetus","a culmination"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “hindrance,” meaning obstacle. “Impetus” (driving force) doesn't fit. “Culmination” (highest point or final result) doesn't fit. “Catalyst” (something that triggers change) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ccb0919015","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-249","passage":"<p>Only students with ______ grades are considered for the prestigious scholarship.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["exceptional","bizarre","obsolete","routine"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “exceptional,” meaning unusually good. “Obsolete” (no longer in use) doesn't fit. “Bizarre” (very strange) doesn't fit. “Routine” (regular and ordinary) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b1b579fac4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-250","passage":"<p>It is unkind to ______ other people's hobbies simply because you do not share them.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["exhort","disparage","extol","lament"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “disparage,” meaning speak of as unimportant. “Exhort” (strongly urge) doesn't fit. “Lament” (express sorrow over) doesn't fit. “Extol” (praise enthusiastically) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.838cc617da","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-251","passage":"<p>The ______ umbrella turned inside out at the first strong gust of wind.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["bulky","flimsy","sturdy","compact"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “flimsy,” meaning weak and easily damaged. “Compact” (small and efficiently arranged) doesn't fit. “Bulky” (large and awkward) doesn't fit. “Sturdy” (strong and solid) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.657cbeaad5","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-253","passage":"<p>Because of the storm, officials decided to ______ the game until next Saturday.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["postpone","approve","cancel","reject"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “postpone,” meaning delay until later. “Reject” (refuse to accept) doesn't fit. “Approve” (accept as satisfactory) doesn't fit. “Cancel” (call off completely) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.5c3f1651ce","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-257","passage":"<p>The bookshelf arrives in pieces, and customers must ______ it themselves.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["separate","assemble","scatter","gather"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “assemble,” meaning put together. “Scatter” (spread in different directions) doesn't fit. “Gather” (collect) doesn't fit. “Separate” (divide into parts) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.1b574dd9e7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-259","passage":"<p>Astronomers will ______ the comet through telescopes as it passes Earth.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["recall","observe","predict","ignore"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “observe,” meaning watch carefully. “Recall” (remember) doesn't fit. “Predict” (say what will happen) doesn't fit. “Ignore” (pay no attention to) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ae28bc7eba","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-264","passage":"<p>Without documents to ______ her claim, the court could not rule in her favor.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["speculate","substantiate","refute","fabricate"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “substantiate,” meaning provide evidence for. “Fabricate” (make up falsely) doesn't fit. “Speculate” (form a theory without firm evidence) doesn't fit. “Refute” (prove wrong) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.fbe2a3bc56","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-266","passage":"<p>Smoking has ______ effects on nearly every organ in the body.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["innocuous","salutary","deleterious","noxious"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “deleterious,” meaning harmful. “Salutary” (beneficial) doesn't fit. “Noxious” (poisonous or very unpleasant) doesn't fit. “Innocuous” (harmless) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.51ce316cf8","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-268","passage":"<p>Critics dismissed him as a ______ who dabbled in painting, poetry, and music without mastering any of them.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["dilettante","novice","prolific","virtuoso"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “dilettante,” meaning amateur with superficial interest. “Prolific” (producing much) doesn't fit. “Virtuoso” (highly skilled performer) doesn't fit. “Novice” (beginner) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.4411cc3251","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-269","passage":"<p>She was hired to ______ the Japanese manual into English.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["summarize","interpret","memorize","translate"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “translate,” meaning express in another language. “Memorize” (learn by heart) doesn't fit. “Interpret” (explain the meaning of) doesn't fit. “Summarize” (give a brief statement of the main points) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.db84624305","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-270","passage":"<p>Her ______ 1990 essay predicted smartphones and social media decades before they existed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["circumspect","myopic","nostalgic","prescient"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “prescient,” meaning having knowledge of events before they happen. “Myopic” (lacking foresight) doesn't fit. “Nostalgic” (longing for the past) doesn't fit. “Circumspect” (cautious and careful) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.2edb46166d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-274","passage":"<p>A ______ of the local theater, he has attended every opening night for forty years.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["sycophant","maverick","pariah","stalwart"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “stalwart,” meaning loyal supporter. “Pariah” (outcast) doesn't fit. “Sycophant” (someone who flatters to gain favor) doesn't fit. “Maverick” (independent-minded person) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.bbb7470353","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-279","passage":"<p>The ______ hostess made every guest feel welcome, even those who arrived uninvited.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["gracious","distant","fickle","loyal"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “gracious,” meaning courteous and kind. “Loyal” (faithful) doesn't fit. “Fickle” (changing loyalties often) doesn't fit. “Distant” (emotionally cool) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.c618113479","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-282","passage":"<p>Publishers chose to ______ the long novel, cutting it to half its original length for young readers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["abridge","elucidate","embellish","obfuscate"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “abridge,” meaning shorten. “Elucidate” (explain clearly) doesn't fit. “Embellish” (add details, often false) doesn't fit. “Obfuscate” (make unclear) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.748c9d0d0f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-285","passage":"<p>The library will ______ laptops to students for up to two weeks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["lend","borrow","donate","purchase"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “lend,” meaning give temporarily. “Donate” (give to a cause) doesn't fit. “Purchase” (buy) doesn't fit. “Borrow” (take temporarily) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.f60d0eb7c9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-287","passage":"<p>Without counting, can you ______ how many people are in the crowd?</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["verify","assume","estimate","measure"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “estimate,” meaning roughly calculate. “Measure” (find the exact size of) doesn't fit. “Assume” (suppose without proof) doesn't fit. “Verify” (check that something is true) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.d35afdc7a8","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-294","passage":"<p>Technology is not ______ that will solve every problem in education.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["an antidote","a palliative","a placebo","a panacea"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “panacea,” meaning cure-all. “Placebo” (substance with no active effect) doesn't fit. “Antidote” (remedy for poison) doesn't fit. “Palliative” (relieving symptoms without curing) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b5d26c5f3e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data6-294","passage":"<p>Hospitals stock ______ for snake venom so bite victims can be treated quickly.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a panacea","an antidote","a placebo","a palliative"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “antidote,” meaning remedy for poison. “Panacea” (cure-all) doesn't fit. “Palliative” (relieving symptoms without curing) doesn't fit. “Placebo” (substance with no active effect) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.418d362eac","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-296","passage":"<p>The results were ______ across all five trials, with nearly identical measurements each time.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["definitive","consistent","anomalous","preliminary"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “consistent,” meaning unchanging in pattern. “Anomalous” (deviating from what is normal) doesn't fit. “Definitive” (conclusive and final) doesn't fit. “Preliminary” (coming before the main part) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.3595b288d1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-299","passage":"<p>When temperatures drop below zero, water trapped in cracks can ______ and split the rock apart.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["freeze","erupt","deposit","erode"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “freeze,” meaning turn to ice. “Deposit” (lay down material) doesn't fit. “Erode” (wear away gradually) doesn't fit. “Erupt” (burst out suddenly) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b9ab031ce1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-300","passage":"<p>Reports of the rare bird have been ______, with only a handful of sightings each decade.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["endemic","incidental","prevalent","sporadic"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “sporadic,” meaning occurring occasionally. “Endemic” (native to a particular place) doesn't fit. “Prevalent” (widespread) doesn't fit. “Incidental” (occurring as a minor consequence) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.cad70a59ae","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-302","passage":"<p>The physicist's work is purely ______; she develops equations but never runs laboratory tests.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["empirical","anecdotal","hypothetical","theoretical"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “theoretical,” meaning based on ideas rather than practice. “Empirical” (based on observation or experiment) doesn't fit. “Hypothetical” (imagined as an example) doesn't fit. “Anecdotal” (based on personal accounts) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ee17d0411a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-303","passage":"<p>The city's ______ district is filled with factories, warehouses, and rail yards.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["agrarian","industrial","urban","nomadic"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “industrial,” meaning relating to manufacturing. “Nomadic” (moving from place to place) doesn't fit. “Urban” (relating to cities) doesn't fit. “Agrarian” (relating to farming) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.402f46414d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-310","passage":"<p>Critics dismissed the painter's early work as ______, noting that it closely copied the styles of her teachers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["evocative","ornate","understated","derivative"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “derivative,” meaning lacking originality. “Ornate” (elaborately decorated) doesn't fit. “Understated” (subtle and restrained) doesn't fit. “Evocative” (bringing strong images to mind) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ab5dd386ef","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-311","passage":"<p>The story's ______ is a greedy landowner who tries to take the farmer's land.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["protagonist","narrator","antagonist","audience"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “antagonist,” meaning character who opposes the main character. “Audience” (people who watch or read) doesn't fit. “Protagonist” (main character) doesn't fit. “Narrator” (person who tells the story) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.c636fa6b12","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-314","passage":"<p>The company offers a bonus as ______ for employees to reach their sales goals.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["a liability","a deterrent","an incentive","an asset"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “incentive,” meaning something that encourages action. “Liability” (legal responsibility) doesn't fit. “Deterrent” (something that discourages action) doesn't fit. “Asset” (something valuable) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b1e5f05fbb","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-316","passage":"<p>Trees in a crowded forest are ______, racing each other to reach sunlight.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["competitive","dormant","parasitic","symbiotic"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “competitive,” meaning striving against others. “Symbiotic” (mutually beneficial) doesn't fit. “Dormant” (temporarily inactive) doesn't fit. “Parasitic” (benefiting at another's expense) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a24f6a0d19","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-318","passage":"<p>Teamwork is ______ to the program; students cannot complete the course alone.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["ostensible","tangential","covert","integral"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “integral,” meaning essential to the whole. “Covert” (hidden) doesn't fit. “Ostensible” (apparent but not necessarily real) doesn't fit. “Tangential” (only slightly related) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.a9921353c9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-319","passage":"<p>After the festival, crews began to ______ the stage piece by piece.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["reinforce","construct","collapse","dismantle"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “dismantle,” meaning take apart. “Collapse” (fall down) doesn't fit. “Construct” (build) doesn't fit. “Reinforce” (strengthen) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.1d1aff5c66","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-319","passage":"<p>Heavy snow caused the barn's roof to ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["reinforce","collapse","dismantle","construct"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “collapse,” meaning fall down. “Dismantle” (take apart) doesn't fit. “Construct” (build) doesn't fit. “Reinforce” (strengthen) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.213e59a79d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-320","passage":"<p>The poet does not name the war directly but seems to ______ to it through images of smoke and ruins.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["juxtapose","delineate","conflate","allude"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “allude,” meaning refer indirectly. “Juxtapose” (place side by side for contrast) doesn't fit. “Delineate” (describe precisely) doesn't fit. “Conflate” (combine two distinct things as one) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.2ce9569622","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-326","passage":"<p>With its white sand and turquoise water, the beach is the ______ of a tropical paradise.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["anachronism","vestige","epitome","harbinger"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “epitome,” meaning perfect example. “Vestige” (trace of something that no longer exists) doesn't fit. “Harbinger” (sign of what is to come) doesn't fit. “Anachronism” (something out of its proper time) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7fd8895a03","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-327","passage":"<p>The ______ distance is ten miles, give or take a few hundred feet.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["relative","precise","absolute","approximate"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “approximate,” meaning close but not exact. “Precise” (exact) doesn't fit. “Relative” (considered in comparison) doesn't fit. “Absolute” (total and complete) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9e35921538","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-327","passage":"<p>The house is small ______ to the others on the street, but it is still larger than most apartments.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["approximate","precise","relative","absolute"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “relative,” meaning considered in comparison. “Absolute” (total and complete) doesn't fit. “Precise” (exact) doesn't fit. “Approximate” (close but not exact) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.154b64fbf2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-330","passage":"<p>Parents often take ______ pleasure in their children's successes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["visceral","vicarious","cerebral","tactile"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “vicarious,” meaning experienced through another person. “Visceral” (felt deeply, as a gut reaction) doesn't fit. “Cerebral” (intellectual rather than emotional) doesn't fit. “Tactile” (relating to touch) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.750fd04730","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-332","passage":"<p>Planned ______ means that some products are designed to become outdated within a few years.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["proliferation","attrition","obsolescence","scarcity"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “obsolescence,” meaning process of becoming outdated. “Proliferation” (rapid increase) doesn't fit. “Scarcity” (shortage) doesn't fit. “Attrition” (gradual reduction) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.cf3d3002d4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-332","passage":"<p>The company reduced its workforce through ______, simply not replacing employees who retired.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["obsolescence","scarcity","proliferation","attrition"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “attrition,” meaning gradual reduction. “Proliferation” (rapid increase) doesn't fit. “Obsolescence” (process of becoming outdated) doesn't fit. “Scarcity” (shortage) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.b276580c02","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-333","passage":"<p>Birds are a recurring ______ in the poet's work, appearing in nearly every poem.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["setting","theme","symbol","motif"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “motif,” meaning repeated element in a work. “Theme” (central message) doesn't fit. “Symbol” (something that represents an idea) doesn't fit. “Setting” (time and place of a story) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.e0f85a4a90","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-333","passage":"<p>The ______ of the novel is a small fishing village in 1850s Maine.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["symbol","setting","motif","theme"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “setting,” meaning time and place of a story. “Symbol” (something that represents an idea) doesn't fit. “Motif” (repeated element in a work) doesn't fit. “Theme” (central message) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.ca4c5f6ec3","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data7-336","passage":"<p>With new evidence supporting it, the once-dismissed theory now seems ______.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["culpable","tenable","untenable","laudable"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “tenable,” meaning able to be defended. “Culpable” (deserving blame) doesn't fit. “Untenable” (unable to be defended) doesn't fit. “Laudable” (deserving praise) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.94b54f6911","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-342","passage":"<p>These hiking boots are so ______ that they have lasted ten years of rough trails.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["flexible","durable","transparent","fragile"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “durable,” meaning long-lasting. “Flexible” (easily bent) doesn't fit. “Fragile” (easily broken) doesn't fit. “Transparent” (see-through) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.0f72279cac","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-344","passage":"<p>The suspect continued to ______ any involvement in the robbery.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["infer","deny","declare","imply"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “deny,” meaning say something is untrue. “Imply” (suggest without saying directly) doesn't fit. “Infer” (conclude from evidence) doesn't fit. “Declare” (state officially) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.9c22c42e7a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-346","passage":"<p>The ad tries to ______ viewers to buy a new car.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["discourage","entertain","inform","persuade"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “persuade,” meaning convince. “Discourage” (try to prevent) doesn't fit. “Inform” (give facts to) doesn't fit. “Entertain” (amuse) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.0613fcc2cc","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-350","passage":"<p>The recipe is ______, requiring only three ingredients and five minutes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["casual","elaborate","simple","formal"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “simple,” meaning plain and easy. “Casual” (relaxed and informal) doesn't fit. “Formal” (following official rules) doesn't fit. “Elaborate” (detailed and complicated) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.76b4e99377","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-353","passage":"<p>The ______ of car horns, sirens, and jackhammers made it impossible to think.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["cacophony","euphony","reverie","tirade"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The context calls for “cacophony,” meaning harsh mix of sounds. “Tirade” (long angry speech) doesn't fit. “Euphony” (pleasant sound) doesn't fit. “Reverie” (daydream) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.6eec52bba5","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-358","passage":"<p>The ice on the sidewalk is a ______, so the school salted it before students arrived.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["shelter","barrier","remedy","hazard"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “hazard,” meaning danger. “Shelter” (protection) doesn't fit. “Barrier” (obstacle) doesn't fit. “Remedy” (cure or solution) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.7c7c2b5783","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-359","passage":"<p>Posting the angry message online was ______, and he quickly regretted it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["nefarious","innocuous","judicious","injudicious"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “injudicious,” meaning unwise. “Judicious” (showing good judgment) doesn't fit. “Nefarious” (wicked) doesn't fit. “Innocuous” (harmless) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.4c04c289d5","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-360","passage":"<p>To ______ water during the drought, residents were asked to take shorter showers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["recycle","consume","generate","conserve"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “conserve,” meaning protect from waste. “Consume” (use up) doesn't fit. “Recycle” (convert waste for reuse) doesn't fit. “Generate” (produce) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.5366ba857d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-365","passage":"<p>His knee injury will ______ him from playing in Saturday's game.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["obviate","preclude","necessitate","exempt"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The context calls for “preclude,” meaning prevent from happening. “Exempt” (free from an obligation) doesn't fit. “Obviate” (remove the need for) doesn't fit. “Necessitate” (make necessary) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.d56f7902f2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-367","passage":"<p>The empire reached its ______ in the second century, controlling more territory than ever before.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["crux","nadir","zenith","facade"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “zenith,” meaning highest point. “Nadir” (lowest point) doesn't fit. “Facade” (false front) doesn't fit. “Crux” (central point) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.086bc9177f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-369","passage":"<p>Many students ______ a summer vacation to take extra classes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["abjure","aver","forgo","countenance"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The context calls for “forgo,” meaning do without. “Aver” (state firmly) doesn't fit. “Countenance” (tolerate or approve) doesn't fit. “Abjure” (formally give up) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.75c617d625","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-372","passage":"<p>The bakery plans to ______ by opening two more locations next year.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["compress","stretch","shrink","expand"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “expand,” meaning grow larger. “Stretch” (extend by pulling) doesn't fit. “Compress” (press together into less space) doesn't fit. “Shrink” (become smaller) doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.words-in-context.2.064ce1adfe","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"words-in-context","difficulty":2,"tmpl":"rw_wic.build","group":"wic-wic_data8-372","passage":"<p>Before running, athletes ______ their leg muscles to prevent injury.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["compress","shrink","expand","stretch"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The context calls for “stretch,” meaning extend by pulling. “Compress” (press together into less space) doesn't fit. “Expand” (grow larger) doesn't fit. “Shrink” (become smaller) doesn't fit."}
